{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A k-d tree: a fixed set of points in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"k"}]},{"type":"text","text":" dimensions that finds the points nearest a query, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"within a radius or a box of it, without testing every point."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"k-d trees","generated":true,"anchor":"k-d-trees","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/BoundingBox"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/init()","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/init(checked:)"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/indices(in:)","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/indices(within:of:)","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/nearestIndex(to:)","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/nearestIndices(to:count:)"]},{"title":"Subscripts","generated":true,"anchor":"Subscripts","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/subscript(checked:)"]},{"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/BidirectionalCollection-Implementations","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/Collection-Implementations","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/ExpressibleByArrayLiteral-Implementations","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/RandomAccessCollection-Implementations","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/Sequence-Implementations"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/ST"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KDTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Point","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Point","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SIMD","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SIMDP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Point","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Scalar","preciseIdentifier":"s:s11SIMDStorageP6ScalarQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FloatingPoint","preciseIdentifier":"s:SF","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tree splits the points at the median of one coordinate, then splits each half at the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"median of the next coordinate, cycling through the dimensions (Bentley, “Multidimensional","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Binary Search Trees Used for Associative Searching”, 1975). It is stored with no links: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"points are permuted so that every subtree is a contiguous run with its median in the middle.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A search descends toward the query and visits the far side of a split only when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"splitting plane is closer than what it has found (Friedman, Bentley and Finkel, 1977).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let tree = KDTree<SIMD2<Double>>([[2, 3], [5, 4], [9, 6], [4, 7], [8, 1], [7, 2]])","tree.nearestIndex(to: [9, 2])                    \/\/ 4: the point [8, 1]","tree.nearestIndices(to: [9, 2], count: 2)        \/\/ [4, 5]","tree.indices(within: 3, of: [5, 5])              \/\/ [1, 3]","tree.indices(in: BoundingBox(lower: [0, 0], upper: [5, 5]))   \/\/ [0, 1]"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Points are SIMD vectors of floating-point scalars, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"SIMD2<Double>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a point in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plane and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SIMD3<Float>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" one in space; distances are Euclidean. As a collection, a k-d tree’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements are its points in the order they were given, and searches answer with their indices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"KDTree","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KDTree"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree.swift#L25","fileNa